      "nav": true,
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "s-hero",
          "type": "profile",
          "title": "",
          "body": "I work in the **MLAI Lab** (Machine Learning & Artificial Intelligence Lab) with Professor Sung Ju Hwang. My research centers on generative weight-space learning, neural network synthesis, and AutoML: encoding pretrained model weights into structured latent representations, generative modeling over those representations (diffusion, flow matching, autoregressive models, VAEs), and transfer across architectures. The long-term goal is a generative AutoML system that synthesizes high-performing network weights directly from architectural specifications, reducing training cost and making model development more accessible.\n\nI received my PhD from KAIST in February 2026 with the thesis *Weight-Space Learning as a Foundation for Deep AutoML*."
        },
